# GENERATED, AND UNMERGEABLE BY HAND.
#
# A place file is a megabyte of coordinates and base64 heights. If two branches
# both regenerate one, git will hand back a conflict no person can resolve —
# and resolving it by picking a side is right, because the file is not authored,
# it is produced by tools/site.mjs from public data.
#
# Marked binary so git stops pretending a three-way text merge is meaningful,
# and union-free so a conflict is an obvious "regenerate this" rather than a
# corrupted hybrid that still parses.
places/*.json -diff -merge
study.json    -diff -merge
site-fit.json -diff -merge
